all : Kendall Tau correlation coefficient\n10972 |             * spearman : Spearman rank correlation\n10973 |             * callable: callable with input two 1d ndarrays\n10974 |                 and returning a float. Note that the returned matrix from corr\n10975 |                 will have 1 along the diagonals and will be symmetric\n10976 |                 regardless of the callable's behavior.\n10977 |         min_periods : int, optional\n10978 |             Minimum number of observations required per pair of columns\n10979 |             to have a valid result. Currently only available for Pearson\n10980 |             and Spearman correlation.\n10981 |         numeric_only : bool, default False\n10982 |             Include only `float`, `int` or `boolean` data.\n10983 | \n10984 |             .. versionadded:: 1.5.0\n10985 | \n10986 |             .. versionchanged:: 2.0.0\n10987 |                 The default value of ``numeric_only`` is now ``False``.\n10988 | \n10989 |         Returns\n10990 |         -------\n10991 |         DataFrame\n10992 |             Correlation matrix.\n10993 | \n10994 |         See Also\n10995 |         --------\n10996 |         DataFrame.corrwith : Compute pairwise correlation with another\n10997 |             DataFrame or Series.\n10998 |         Series.corr : Compute the correlation between two Series.\n10999 | \n11000 |         Notes\n11001 |         -----\n11002 |         Pearson, Kendall and Spearman correlation are currently computed using pairwise complete observations.\n11003 | \n11004 |         * `Pearson correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11005 |         * `Kendall rank correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendall_rank_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11006 |         * `Spearman's rank correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spearman%27s_rank_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11007 | \n11008 |         Examples\n11009 |         --------\n11010 |     