Array, DatetimeIndex or Series\n1162 |             The same type as the original data. Series will have the same\n1163 |             name and index. DatetimeIndex will have the same name.\n1164 | \n1165 |         See Also\n1166 |         --------\n1167 |         floor : Floor the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1168 |         ceil : Ceil the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1169 |         round : Round the datetimes to the specified freq.\n1170 | \n1171 |         Examples\n1172 |         --------\n1173 |         >>> idx = pd.date_range(\n1174 |         ...     start=\"2014-08-01 10:00\", freq=\"h\", periods=3, tz=\"Asia/Calcutta\"\n1175 |         ... )\n1176 |         >>> idx\n1177 |         DatetimeIndex(['2014-08-01 10:00:00+05:30',\n1178 |                        '2014-08-01 11:00:00+05:30',\n1179 |                        '2014-08-01 12:00:00+05:30'],\n1180 |                         dtype='datetime64[ns, Asia/Calcutta]', freq='h')\n1181 |         >>> idx.normalize()\n1182 |         DatetimeIndex(['2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30',\n1183 |                        '2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30',\n1184 |                        '2014-08-01 00:00:00+05:30'],\n1185 |                        dtype='datetime64[ns, Asia/Calcutta]', freq=None)\n1186 |         \"\"\"\n1187 |         new_values = normalize_i8_timestamps(self.asi8, self.tz, reso=self._creso)\n1188 |         dt64_values = new_values.view(self._ndarray.dtype)\n1189 | \n1190 |         dta = type(self)._simple_new(dt64_values, dtype=dt64_values.dtype)\n1191 |         dta = dta._with_freq(\"infer\")\n1192 |         if self.tz is not None:\n1193 |             dta = dta.tz_localize(self.tz)\n1194 |         return dta\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/series.py:Series.round`.\nFound function `pandas/core/frame.py:DataFrame.round`.\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.round`.\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/managers.py:BaseBlockManager.round`.\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/masked.py:BaseMaskedA